Add an "X" close button to popup-style panels.

Currently the Settings, Help (?), Sample Browser, and Pattern
Presets panels can only be dismissed via the toolbar toggles —
there is no in-panel close affordance, which is unusual UX.

Affected files (ImGui frontend):
- src/gui/settings_panel.cpp:87 — uses NoTitleBar, no p_open
- src/gui/sample_browser.cpp:227-230 — uses NoTitleBar, no p_open
- src/gui/pattern_presets.cpp:428 — already passes &open, verify X
- Help/About panel — find and update

Either drop NoTitleBar so ImGui draws the standard title+X (and
keep NoCollapse), or render a manual X button in the top-right
corner of each panel that toggles the same global show flag the
toolbar uses.

Note: TASK-145 (sample-browser-exit-button) was marked done but
the user reports this is still missing — re-verify and reopen if
needed.

## Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] Settings panel shows an X in its top-right corner
- [ ] Sample Browser panel shows an X in its top-right corner
- [ ] Pattern Presets panel shows an X in its top-right corner
- [ ] Help (?) panel shows an X in its top-right corner
- [ ] Clicking X toggles off the same flag as the toolbar
- [ ] Apply same change to GTK frontend (frontend parity rule)

## Test Plan
- [ ] Open each panel via toolbar, close via X, verify state
- [ ] Reopen via toolbar, verify panel restores cleanly
- [ ] Verify no double-close issues if both X and toolbar toggled
